SupraLINUX integrates the signed official stable KDE Plasma 6.7.5 source with
Ubuntu 26.04 packaging. Preserve all 21 binaries (including original transitional
packages), five SONAMEs, symbols, QML modules, sensor-face packages, process
plugins and KAuth/network helpers. Ubuntu Qt 6.10 providers remain unchanged.

Enable all eight official native CTests. A private typed sensor provider supplies
the versioned SDK service and the legacy upstream presence-check alias. Candidate
headers/plugins/packages are used at build time. Privilege-dependent process cases
may retain upstream QSKIP behavior and must be reported separately in the logs.

The installed Ubuntu ABI contract exercises formatting, an owned process with
memory and termination transitions, real private D-Bus sensors and model signals,
SystemStats property/object lifecycle, installed SensorFace package/configuration,
QML creation and software rendering. Both original Ubuntu-built executables are
retained unchanged across normal APT upgrade. An exact 6.7.5 installed SDK consumer
is compiled separately. Local Ubuntu prototype PASS does not certify the candidate.

Exact eligible Frameworks artifacts include the reviewed transitive DAG closure;
original historical verification scopes remain unchanged. No KDE source patch,
helper privilege change, hardware process control or Qt replacement is introduced.
Full application/session QA, real ksystemstats hardware plugins, GPU/network
capture, privileged helper actions and accelerated/Wayland rendering remain later
integration gates. Initial packaging preparation did not execute the candidate.

Native CTest stdout/stderr are inherited by the retained clean sbuild log, while
installed consumer output remains independently retained in its result files.
HOME is private; cleanup verifies every owned process-group absence.

Revision 4:6.7.5-0supralinux2 adds only the missing candidate source/systemstats
include directory to the native sensor-provider fixture. Attempt 1 remains an
original package FAIL: upstream compilation completed, provider compilation
stopped at generated-header SensorInfo.h lookup, and CTests/lintian/installed
tests did not run. Its sources/logs restore offline and owned KVM cleanup passed.
Local negative/positive include-path reproduction and the original Ubuntu client
with the repaired provider passed, with owned cleanup. This local mechanism uses
actual candidate source/XML and Qt-generated D-Bus headers, plus authenticated
original export-visibility metadata; it does not certify the full candidate build.
Fresh KVM must generate candidate headers and execute all eight official tests,
lintian and unchanged-original/rebuilt installed clients. Source, assertions,
symbol guards, dependency closure, product profile and Qt remain unchanged.
